#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0703 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: BASETYPE is not present, ByIND is populated, and ByIND is not equal to AyIND where ABLFL is equal to Y for a given value of PARAMCD for a combination of device and subject
#note "BASETYPE absent, B1IND=HIGH != A1IND=LOW, ABLFL=Y -> violation"
# Engine-gap G6 (adam-rule-engine-gaps.md) is CLOSED by Fix #152: the wildcard
# token in Operations[].name (AyIND) is now substituted during expansion
# (WildcardExpander.expandRule), so max(A1IND) reads a real column. Before the fix
# this rule fired on every populated row and the valid sibling (CDISC-AD0703-valid-ADLBC.cdt)
# could not pass; it has been restored alongside this one.
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset ADLBC class=MD-BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SPDEVID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ABLFL type=Char
col B1IND type=Char
col A1IND type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | DEV01 | GLUC | Y | HIGH | LOW
---
